## Field check of the shipped week

A read of `apps/storytime/content/l2/w01.json` before the edit confirmed the fields of the flow:

- `opening.pa` holds 5 prompts, each with an English text and a Thai text.
- `scripts` holds 5 lessons. Day 1 holds 8 steps, day 2 holds 7, day 3 holds 7, day 4 holds 6, and
  day 5 holds 5. Every step holds an id, a title, minutes, an English note, a Thai note, and the
  three variant lines.
- `review[]` holds one strip per day. Day 1, day 4, and day 5 hold no card.
- `check.items` holds 4 items. Three items name their pictures, and one item names a letter.

The first step title of each day holds no word of the opening routine, of the review strip, or of
the day title. The step content of no day holds the id of another step of that day. The flow shows
one step on each screen without holding a second step id.

## The implementation

- `apps/storytime/app/[locale]/teacher/[level]/[week]/[day]/lesson-flow.tsx` exports
  `TeacherLessonFlow` with the props `{ week, day, locale }`. The view is a client view with the
  screen state and the Thai state.
- Screen 1 holds the opening routine, the review strip of the day, and the first step. Each later
  screen holds one step. The control "Next step" moves forward, and the last screen holds no such
  control.
- A step screen shows the step id, the step title, `<minutes> min`, the four headings, and the
  three variant lines. The four headings and the three variant labels stay in English, because they
  hold no `{ en, th }` field.
- The last screen of day 5 holds the Friday check. The check shows on day 5 only.
- The control "ไทย" switches every `{ en, th }` field to its Thai text. A field with no Thai text
  keeps its English text.
- Every value comes from the week file. The view holds no string that names a week item. The view
  uses no next-intl hook.
- The new controls use the brand classes of the teacher week view: amber `#fcd34d` with brown
  `#92400e` text for the Thai toggle, and brown `#92400e` with white text for the forward control
  and the way back to the week. No blue class.
- `apps/storytime/app/[locale]/teacher/[level]/[week]/[day]/page.tsx` keeps the order of the
  checks: the session, the teacher switch, the 403 view, the route parse, the week load, and the
  day check. The route renders the flow after the checks.

